module bindings.go.revocationCheckAgainstCurrentTime;

// A revocation list is a map from a subject -- a public key, a key id, a
// certificate serial -- to the instant that subject's credentials stop being
// honoured, and the instant is defined against the *credential*, not against the
// reader: nats-io/jwt documents `RevocationList.Revoke(pubKey, timestamp)` as
// revoking everything issued before that timestamp and hands the check
// `IsRevoked(pubKey, timestamp)` / `IsClaimRevoked(claim)` so the caller supplies
// the claim's own issue time; RFC 5280 5.3.1 dates a CRL entry the same way, and
// an `iat`-keyed JWT denylist is the same construction again.
//
// Comparing the entry against `time.Now()` instead is what breaks it, in both
// directions. An entry dated ahead of the clock never fires, so an already-issued
// credential the operator has revoked keeps authenticating until that date; once
// the clock passes it, the entry fires against credentials minted afterwards that
// the entry was never meant to cover. Either way the revocation list does not say
// what it is documented to say (CWE-287/CWE-613).
//
// Two facts in one Go function body are that shape: a subscript read of a
// revocation-named record, which is the hand-rolled lookup the library APIs above
// exist to replace, and a wall-clock read in the same body. Both are
// function-confined here -- a minimal pair with the subscript in one method and
// `time.Now()` in a sibling labels nothing.
//
// The neutraliser is the credential's own time being in scope: `IssuedAt`, `iat`,
// `NotBefore` or `nbf` named anywhere in the body means the comparison has the
// operand the record is defined against, whether it is spelled inline or passed
// to a helper that does the comparing.
binding goRevocationCheckAgainstCurrentTime {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "go" and containsAny(node.context.index, ["Revok", "revok", "Revoc", "revoc"]) and containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["time.Now"]) and not containsAny(node.context.identifier, ["IssuedAt", "issuedAt", "issued_at", "NotBefore", "notBefore", "not_before"])
  emit issue code.RevocationCheckAgainstCurrentTime at node
}
